{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2008413d-1b80-471a-9971-7f7e6634139d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8915d5e28db295e9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-jt6p83lf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E001.md","content":"# State-driven Kueue workload status model with eviction-reason distinction and message overrides\n\n## Description\n\nRebuild the odh-dashboard workbench status model for Kueue-managed workloads so that scheduling\nstatus is derived statefully from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses instead of\nevent-driven wildcard/substring matching of progress steps. The model distinguishes preemption\nfrom other eviction reasons, surfaces the Requeued retry state, extends the WorkloadCondition type\nunion to match real Kueue condition types, and adds a human-friendly message override lookup with\nan unconditional raw-message fallback.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the `WorkloadCondition` type union in `k8sTypes.ts` to include `QuotaReserved`,\n  `Admitted`, `PodsReady`, `Finished`, `Evicted`, `Preempted`, `Requeued`,\n  `BlockedOnPreemptionGates`, and `DeactivationTarget`. Remove the incorrect `'Failed'` entry —\n  Kueue has no condition type called `Failed`; failure is expressed as `Finished` with reason\n  `Failed`.\n- Distinguish \"Preempted\" (a higher-priority workload took resources) from \"Evicted\" (admin action\n  or timeout) in the workbench status display. Cover the eviction reasons: Preempted,\n  PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated,\n  NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded.\n- Surface the Requeued state with retry count and next retry time computed from `requeueState`\n  when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the queue.\n- Derive status state-driven from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses. Move away\n  from wildcard/substring matching of events to a structured, extensible status derivation model\n  so all workload scheduling information is surfaced.\n- Provide human-friendly message overrides for known condition/reason combinations as a lookup\n  table, populated with reasonable engineering defaults. Always fall back to showing the raw Kueue\n  condition message from the `.message` field — under no circumstance show a blank state when a\n  Kueue condition exists.\n- Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, and surface\n  AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n- Keep all changes purely additive and conditional: existing workbench behavior is unchanged when\n  Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace where a workbench has been evicted due to\n  `ClusterQueueStopped`, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays\n  \"Evicted\" with reason \"Queue stopped by administrator\" — NOT \"Preempted\", measured by the status\n  label text and variant differing from the Preempted state.\n- Given a workbench has been evicted and the Workload CR has a `Requeued` condition with\n  `requeueState.requeueAt` set, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays\n  the retry information including next retry time and attempt count, measured by the status text\n  including the computed retry time from `requeueState`.\n- Given a workbench's Workload CR has a condition type or reason not recognized by the dashboard's\n  status model, when the workbench status is rendered, then the raw Kueue condition message is\n  displayed rather than a blank state, measured by the status text containing the Workload CR's\n  condition `.message` field content.\n- Given a Workload CR contains condition types not yet present in the dashboard's\n  `WorkloadCondition` type union, when the status renders, then those conditions are shown with\n  raw message text and never silently dropped.\n- Status derivation is covered by tests for each eviction reason, the Requeued path,\n  WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, and AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not\n  Kueue-managed (rollback safety for the replaced event-matching logic).\n- The message override table is structured so entries can be replaced with reviewed content\n  without code changes, with reasonable default copy in place until then.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-P0-1: Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons (ClusterQueueStopped,\n  LocalQueueStopped, PodsReadyTimeout, Deactivated, etc.) in the workbench status display.\n- HLR-P0-2: Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState`.\n- HLR-P0-5: Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with\n  human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback.\n- HLR-P2-10: Move away from wildcard/substring event matching to a structured, extensible status\n  derivation model.\n- HLR-P2-11: Improve status message granularity — WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck\n  pending/retry states.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51668,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6568cad8f7b8cd","agent_id":"a105cb301b85439d8","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"cc8ae580-4f7d-459f-b9cc-d6ce51c5952b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:22:50.863Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
