{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2008413d-1b80-471a-9971-7f7e6634139d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4148c9a2fced66d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-jt6p83lf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E002.md","content":"# Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display\n\n## Description\n\nIntegrate Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`) into the odh-dashboard so\nthe workbenches overview can display the queue position of pending workloads\n(`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via the `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on\nLocalQueues, with silent graceful degradation when the user's RBAC does not permit reading it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a frontend API client for the LocalQueue pending-workloads subresource:\n  `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`.\n- All calls go through the existing `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy using the logged-in user's token\n  (browser → frontend SDK → `/api/k8s` → K8s API), so every call is subject to the user's RBAC\n  permissions.\n- Display the queue position (position in local queue) for workbenches in QueuingPending state in\n  the workbenches overview.\n- Handle a 403 on the Visibility API silently using the existing `getGenericErrorCode` pattern\n  from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx` — position info is supplementary, not critical; no error\n  is surfaced to the user.\n- Reuse the existing workload-to-notebook matching (`buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` in\n  `api/k8s/workloads.ts`) to associate pending-workload positions with workbenches.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has `batch-user` RBAC to the\n  Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is displayed\n  (position in local queue), measured by the position number being present and matching the value\n  from the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT have RBAC to the\n  Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is silently\n  omitted with no error displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error\n  indicators.\n- All Visibility API requests are issued through the `/api/k8s` passthrough with the logged-in\n  user's token — no privileged impersonation.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Whether data scientists in RHOAI clusters receive Kubernetes `view`, `edit`, or `batch-user`\n  ClusterRole bindings that aggregate Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` is an open\n  question owned by AI Core Platform. It is non-gating: the code handles 403 gracefully either\n  way. If the bindings are absent, position display is effectively admin-only, which would reduce\n  the value of further position UI polish.\n- Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`) with the `VisibilityOnDemand`\n  feature gate (Beta, enabled by default since Kueue v0.9) is confirmed available in RHBoK shipped\n  with RHOAI 3.5.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51668,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6568cad8f7b8cd","agent_id":"a105cb301b85439d8","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"87ce11f5-e2e1-4c1e-9034-9ac3dfad1963","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:22:59.022Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
