{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2008413d-1b80-471a-9971-7f7e6634139d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93e98589bd8581b7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-jt6p83lf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E003.md","content":"# Kueue management indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n\n## Description\n\nAdd Kueue management visibility to the odh-dashboard UI: a positive indicator on the project\ndetails page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, and an anomaly indicator on workbenches in a\nKueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue. Both indicators render conditionally — no\nUI changes when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Positive Kueue indicator on the project details page, shown when the namespace carries the\n  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, telling users their project uses queue-based\n  scheduling. The exact form (info banner, badge, or label) is a pending UX decision\n  (RHOAIUX-7470); implement with a placeholder treatment that is clearly marked for replacement\n  when the finalized design lands.\n- Anomaly indicator on workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are missing the\n  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (workloads created via GitOps or CLI that bypass Kueue). Do\n  NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every workload in a Kueue-managed namespace — only flag the\n  anomaly.\n- Anomaly detection reuses the namespace `kueue.openshift.io/managed` label and the workload\n  queue-label check; the indicator serves hybrid GitOps + dashboard users.\n- The dashboard remains opinionated (auto-enables Kueue) but explicitly tells users what it is\n  doing; the anomaly indicator never blocks workload creation or any action.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive\n  indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator\n  element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`\n  exists and absent when it does not.\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the\n  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the\n  user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator\n  that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on\n  non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n- The placeholder visual treatments are implemented such that the finalized design treatment can\n  be applied without structural changes to the indicator logic.\n- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not\n  Kueue-managed.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-P0-3: Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has\n  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n- HLR-P0-4: Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed\n  by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51668,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6568cad8f7b8cd","agent_id":"a105cb301b85439d8","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"dc321187-4e4e-453a-8b27-a5298dc06aae","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:07.059Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
