{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2008413d-1b80-471a-9971-7f7e6634139d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a155544e72a14b61","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-jt6p83lf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E004.md","content":"# HardwareProfile form and popover hardening for Kueue\n\n## Description\n\nHarden the odh-dashboard HardwareProfile surfaces for queue-based scheduling: LocalQueue name\nformat validation in the admin form, a fallback path in the HardwareProfile details popover for\nGitOps-managed notebooks whose queue label was applied directly, an explicit explanation on the\nHardwareProfile dropdown in Kueue-managed namespaces, and a non-blocking warning when a referenced\nLocalQueue does not exist at workbench creation time.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add `k8sNameRegex` validation (`/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/`) to the LocalQueue name field\n  in the HardwareProfile admin form. Validation is format-only: existence cannot be checked\n  because HardwareProfiles are cluster-scoped while LocalQueues are namespace-scoped, so the\n  target namespace is unknown at HP creation time.\n- HardwareProfile details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks: when no HP scheduling\n  data exists for a notebook that has `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` applied directly, read the queue\n  label from the notebook's own labels, resolve the cluster queue name from the project's\n  LocalQueue list, and indicate the source — e.g. \"Queue: my-queue (applied directly)\" vs.\n  \"Queue: my-queue (via hardware profile)\".\n- Add an explicit info indicator (info icon or tooltip) on the HardwareProfile dropdown in the\n  workbench creation form when running in a Kueue-managed namespace, explaining that only\n  queue-enabled hardware profiles are shown because the project uses queue-based scheduling. Keep\n  the strict filtering behavior unchanged.\n- At workbench creation time, if the specified LocalQueue does not exist in the target namespace,\n  display a warning — NOT an error. The admin may have intended the LQ to be created later or via\n  GitOps; these are eventually consistent systems and Kueue itself reports the error via the\n  Workload's conditions if the queue truly does not exist. The warning is dismissible and never\n  blocks workbench creation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a GitOps-managed workbench with `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label applied directly (no\n  matching HardwareProfile), when the user opens the HardwareProfile details popover, then the\n  popover displays the queue name with indication it was applied directly (not via hardware\n  profile), measured by the popover text including the queue name and a source indicator.\n- Given an admin is creating a HardwareProfile and enters an invalid LocalQueue name (e.g.\n  contains uppercase or spaces), when the form validates, then a validation error is shown for the\n  LocalQueue name field, measured by the form displaying an inline error referencing the Kubernetes\n  name format.\n- Given a workbench is being created with a HardwareProfile referencing a LocalQueue that does not\n  exist in the target namespace, when the creation form is submitted, then a warning (not error)\n  is displayed indicating the local queue was not found, measured by the warning being dismissible\n  and not blocking workbench creation.\n- Given a workbench is in a Kueue-managed namespace and the user opens the workbench creation\n  form, when the HardwareProfile dropdown renders with only queue-enabled profiles, then an info\n  indicator explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown, measured by the presence of a\n  tooltip or info icon adjacent to the dropdown.\n- The HardwareProfile dropdown continues to show only queue-based hardware profiles in\n  Kueue-managed namespaces (strict filtering behavior retained).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-P1-7: Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks — read queue label\n  directly when no HP match exists, indicate source.\n- HLR-P1-8: Add `k8sNameRegex` validation to LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile admin form.\n- HLR-P1-9: Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled profiles\n  are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51668,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6568cad8f7b8cd","agent_id":"a105cb301b85439d8","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"c10141bd-7a64-4441-bf5a-0597413afef7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:16.937Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
