out code changes.\n- The copy is written for data scientists (non-Kubernetes-experts): raw Kueue condition messages\n  are unintelligible to that audience, which is the motivation for the overrides.\n- Message lengths fit the dashboard status display constraints.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Engineering is not blocked on this deliverable: the dashboard ships reasonable default overrides\n  first, and the reviewed copy replaces them when available.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-P0-5 (supporting): human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status — the\n  override framework and default copy are delivered by the dashboard status model work; this epic\n  delivers the reviewed final wording.\n- HLR-P2-11 (supporting): wording for the improved message granularity (WaitForRecovery vs.\n  WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry states).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55595,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d6568cad8f7b8cd","agent_id":"a105cb301b85439d8","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"12954639-1ace-4d8f-a59b-ccb5a8534b95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:36.123Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
