{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8236f53ed0de1c9c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E005\n3\ttitle: UX design deliverables for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: -1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# UX design deliverables for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDeliver the finalized UX designs for the Kueue workload scheduling visibility features: the visual\n34\ttreatment for the positive Kueue indicator on the project details page, the anomaly indicator\n35\tdesign for non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces, the HardwareProfile dropdown info\n36\tindicator treatment, and the status message content review. Engineering is not blocked on these\n37\tdeliverables — the dashboard ships placeholder treatments first and applies the finalized designs\n38\twhen they arrive.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Decide and document the form of the positive Kueue indicator on the project details page (info\n43\t  banner vs. badge vs. label) for namespaces with `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`, and deliver\n44\t  the visual treatment spec.\n45\t- Design the anomaly indicator for workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are missing the\n46\t  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (the hybrid GitOps + dashboard user case).\n47\t- Design the info indicator tre