k pending/retry\n46\t  states.\n47\t- Structure the deliverable as lookup-table entries keyed by condition/reason, consumable directly\n48\t  by the dashboard's message override table.\n49\t- Complete content review with the UXD team (RHOAIUX-7470).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Override copy is delivered for every known condition/reason combination enumerated by the\n54\t  dashboard status model, each entry keyed by condition type and reason.\n55\t- The copy is reviewed with UXD via RHOAIUX-7470.\n56\t- The deliverable is structured as a lookup table that drops into the dashboard's override\n57\t  mechanism without code changes.\n58\t- The copy is written for data scientists (non-Kubernetes-experts): raw Kueue condition messages\n59\t  are unintelligible to that audience, which is the motivation for the overrides.\n60\t- Message lengths fit the dashboard status display constraints.\n61\t\n62\t## Notes\n63\t\n64\t- Engineering is not blocked on this deliverable: the dashboard ships reasonable default overrides\n65\t  first, and the reviewed copy replaces them when available.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-P0-5 (supporting): human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status — the\n70\t  override framework and default copy are delivered by the dashboard status model work; this epic\n71\t  delivers the reviewed final wording.\n72\t- HLR-P2-11 (supporting): wording for the improved message granularity (WaitForRecovery vs.\n73\t  WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry states).\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c5bb6d534fccb8","agent_id":"a22a3e8dbdab62dfe","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"84af4285-4e82-499e-b081-74978bbbcbf6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:26:35.585Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7f1568eeed7fa70","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decompos