atment (info icon / tooltip) for the HardwareProfile dropdown that\n48\t  explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n49\t- Complete the status message content review (RHOAIUX-7470) jointly with the Content team's\n50\t  microcopy deliverable.\n51\t- Deliver design specs that are implementable in the odh-dashboard without structural redesign of\n52\t  the placeholder implementations.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The design decision for the positive Kueue indicator form is made and documented with\n57\t  rationale, and the visual treatment spec is delivered.\n58\t- The anomaly indicator design is delivered and clearly distinguishes non-Kueue workloads without\n59\t  adding per-workload noise in the steady state.\n60\t- The HardwareProfile dropdown info indicator treatment is delivered.\n61\t- The status message content review (RHOAIUX-7470) is completed.\n62\t- All delivered specs can be applied to the existing placeholder implementations without\n63\t  structural changes to indicator logic.\n64\t\n65\t## Notes\n66\t\n67\t- This epic runs in parallel with dashboard engineering work by design — the strategy explicitly\n68\t  states development must not be blocked on UX answers, since the questions concern microcopy and\n69\t  visual treatment, not major redesigns.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-P0-3 (supporting): visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator on the project details\n74\t  page — the indicator itself is delivered by the dashboard engineering work with placeholder\n75\t  treatment.\n76\t- HLR-P0-4 (supporting): anomaly indicator design for non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed\n77\t  namespaces.\n78\t- HLR-P1-9 (supporting): info indicator treatment for the HardwareProfile dropdown.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b6b36d695fc6a0","agent_id":"ad0e673d5de9c7d11","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"2ad13632-5a2a-4747-a363-7d11f1aeb41a","timesta