{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a35a1ebaaed03126","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E006\n3\ttitle: Status message microcopy for Kueue condition/reason overrides (RHOAIUX-7470)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: Content\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Status message microcopy for Kueue condition/reason overrides (RHOAIUX-7470)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAuthor the human-readable status message wording — the override copy for known Kueue\n34\tcondition/reason combinations displayed in the workbench status — replacing the engineering\n35\tdefault copy once content review is complete. Raw Kueue condition messages remain the fallback for\n36\tuncovered combinations; this content supplements that fallback, never replaces it.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Write human-friendly override messages for the known Kueue condition/reason combinations,\n41\t  including the eviction reasons (Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped,\n42\t  LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded), distinguishing\n43\t  \"Preempted\" (higher-priority workload took resources) from \"Evicted\" (admin action or timeout).\n44\t- Write copy for the Requeued retry state (retry count and next retry time presentation).\n45\t- Write copy distinguishing WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, and for AdmissionCheck pending/retry\n46\t  states.\n47\t- Structure the deliverable as lookup-table entries keyed by condition/reason, consumable directly\n48\t  by the dashboard's message override table.\n49\t- Complete content review with the UXD team (RHOAIUX-7470).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Override copy is delivered for every known condition/reason combination enumerated by the\n54\t  dashboard status model, each entry keyed by condition type and reason.\n55\t- The copy is reviewed with UXD via RHOAIUX-7470.\n56\t- The deliverable is structured as a lookup table that drops into the dashboard's override\n57\t  mechanism without code changes.\n58\t- The copy is written for data scientists (non-Kubernetes-experts): raw Kueue condition messages\n59\t  are unintelligible to that audience, which is the motivation for the overrides.\n60\t- Message lengths fit the dashboard status display constraints.\n61\t\n62\t## Notes\n63\t\n64\t- Engineering is not blocked on this deliverable: the dashboard ships reasonable default overrides\n65\t  first, and the reviewed copy replaces them when available.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-P0-5 (supporting): human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status — the\n70\t  override framework and default copy are delivered by the dashboard status model work; this epic\n71\t  delivers the reviewed final wording.\n72\t- HLR-P2-11 (supporting): wording for the improved message granularity (WaitForRecovery vs.\n73\t  WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry states).\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b6b36d695fc6a0","agent_id":"ad0e673d5de9c7d11","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"260f41ab-8817-4b98-b91f-742d99bc0d83","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:38.173Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a35a1ebaaed03126","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
