{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90d103bb194af739","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition: RHAISTRAT-8002 — Integrate Kueue Workload Scheduling Information in Workbenches Overview\n10\t\n11\t## Triage Outcome\n12\t\n13\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is S-sized and bounded to a\n14\tsingle code component (odh-dashboard), but it is not single-team: the Impacted Teams list commits\n15\tfour teams (Dashboard UI, UXD, Content, Docs), and the scope spans multiple distinct work streams —\n16\tfrontend code implementation, UX design authoring (RHOAIUX-7470), substantive microcopy content\n17\tauthoring, and documentation (Documentation Support is required). The multiple-distinct-work-streams\n18\tescape condition fires, so below-threshold does not apply.\n19\t\n20\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (Step 1.5)\n21\t\n22\tThe Staff Engineer / SME Input section is non-empty and takes precedence over the AI-generated\n23\tstrategy sections. Overrides applied:\n24\t\n25\t1. **Component scope**: only odh-dashboard is affected. rhods-operator was removed from the\n26\t   affected components — its HardwareProfile mutating webhook injects the\n27\t   `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label on Notebook CRs and is explicitly out of this STRAT.\n28\t2. **AI-generated \"Proposed Solution\" superseded**: the original solution section's resource\n29\t   columns (\"Requested vs. available CPU/GPU/Memory\"), estimated wait time indicators, historical\n30\t   queue data, and policy information panels are not in the committed HLR list and are out of\n31\t   scope. LocalQueues carry no quota information (quota lives at the ClusterQueue level, often\n32\t   unreadable by data scientists), and Kueue provides no wait-time prediction — only factual\n33\t   elapsed wait time.\n34\t3. **Status model approach**: state-driven from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses,\n35\t   never event-driven from hardcoded progress steps or wildcard/substring event matching. Raw\n36\t   Kueue condition message is always the fallback — never a blank state.\n37\t4. **Non-blocking UX**: development must not block on UXD answers (RHOAIUX-7470). Placeholder\n38\t   copy/treatment ships first; finalized content replaces it later.\n39\t\n40\t## Component Mappings\n41\t\n42\t| Strategy component | Canonical component (`submit.py` vocabulary) | Notes |\n43\t|---|---|---|\n44\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Architecture context file exists (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`) — component is in the platform; no onboarding chain. |\n45\t| UXD design + Content microcopy deliverables (RHOAIUX-7470) | UXD | Delivered via the UXD work stream; no separate Content component exists in the canonical list. |\n46\t| Documentation deliverable | Documentation | Docs team release note / feature docs. |\n47\t\n48\tPassive components: kueue-operator (architecture context exists) requires no code changes — the\n49\tVisibility API is consumed read-only through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s` passthrough.\n50\tValidation of its behavior (including 403 handling) is captured as acceptance criteria on the\n51\tVisibility API epic. No separate team validates it, so no standalone validation epic is generated.\n52\t\n53\t## Investigation Evaluation (Step 3)\n54\t\n55\tAll unknowns were scanned (open questions table, risks, assumptions). Neither qualifies as an\n56\tInvestigation epic:\n57\t\n58\t- **Visibility API RBAC for data scientists** (open question, owner AI Core Platform): the\n59\t  strategy itself resolves the engineering response — code handles 403 gracefully either way, so\n60\t  the answer does not change which epics exist or what they build; it only affects how much polish\n61\t  to invest in the position UI. Modeled as an acceptance criterion (silent 403 degradation) plus a\n62\t  health warning below.\n63\t- **Form of the positive Kueue indicator** (open question, owner UXD / RHOAIUX-7470): a design\n64\t  deliverable produced by an impacted team inside this strategy, explicitly non-blocking\n65\t  (placeholder treatment first). Modeled as a parallel Implementation epic owned by UXD, with a\n66\t  downstream integration epic — not an Investigation.\n67\t\n68\t## Epic List\n69\t\n70\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n71\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n72\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | State-driven Kueue workload status model with eviction-reason distinction and message overrides | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue management indicators on project details and workbenches overview | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile form and popover hardening for Kueue | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | UX design deliverables for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | UXD | P1 |\n77\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | Status message microcopy for Kueue condition/reason overrides (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | Content | P1 |\n78\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Integrate finalized Kueue UX designs and content into the dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n79\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E008 | Documentation for Kueue workload scheduling visibility | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P1 |\n80\t\n81\t## Dependency DAG\n82\t\n83\t```mermaid\n84\tgraph TD\n85\t  E001[\"E001 Status model (P0)\"]\n86\t  E002[\"E002 Visibility API queue position (P1)\"]\n87\t  E003[\"E003 Kueue indicators (P0)\"]\n88\t  E004[\"E004 HP form hardening (P1)\"]\n89\t  E005[\"E005 UX design deliverables (P1)\"]\n90\t  E006[\"E006 Status message microcopy (P1)\"]\n91\t  E007[\"E007 Integrate finalized UX/content (P1)\"]\n92\t  E008[\"E008 Documentation (P1)\"]\n93\t  E001 --> E007\n94\t  E003 --> E007\n95\t  E004 --> E007\n96\t  E005 --> E007\n97\t  E006 --> E007\n98\t  E001 --> E008\n99\t  E002 --> E008\n100\t  E003 --> E008\n101\t  E004 --> E008\n102\t  E005 --> E008\n103\t  E006 --> E008\n104\t  E007 --> E008\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\t## DAG Justification\n108\t\n109\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n110\t|---|---|---|\n111\t| (none among E001–E006) | 14, 15 | E001–E004 live in the same repo but in different areas (status derivation logic, API client, page-level indicators, forms) — parallel; merge coordination is a risk note, not a dependency. E005/E006 are different teams with independent inputs — parallel. No epic builds against an artifact another of these produces. |\n112\t| E001 → E007 | 13 | The integration epic swaps the default message-override entries delivered by the status model — it builds against that lookup table. |\n113\t| E003 → E007 | 13 | Final visual treatments are applied to the indicator surfaces delivered by the indicators work. |\n114\t| E004 → E007 | 13 | The HP dropdown info indicator's final treatment is applied to the form surface delivered by the HP hardening work. |\n115\t| E005 → E007 | 13 | Integration consumes the finalized design deliverable (build-against artifact: design spec). |\n116\t| E006 → E007 | 13 | Integration consumes the reviewed microcopy deliverable (build-against artifact: override table content). |\n117\t| E002 ∥ E007 (no edge) | 14 | Queue position display is not UX-gated; no build-against artifact shared. |\n118\t| E001–E007 → E008 | 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy — docs describe what was built. |\n119\t\n120\tNo repo-onboarding, license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics: odh-dashboard is in the\n121\tplatform (architecture context file exists) and no new component or container image is provis