{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b028fc677f68cfc5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition: RHAISTRAT-8002 — Integrate Kueue Workload Scheduling Information in Workbenches Overview\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is S-sized and bounded to a\n15\tsingle code component (odh-dashboard), but it is not single-team: the Impacted Teams list commits\n16\tfour teams (Dashboard UI, UXD, Content, Docs), and the scope spans multiple distinct work streams —\n17\tfrontend code implementation, UX design authoring (RHOAIUX-7470), substantive microcopy content\n18\tauthoring, and documentation (Documentation Support is required). The multiple-distinct-work-streams\n19\tescape condition fires, so below-threshold does not apply.\n20\t\n21\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (Step 1.5)\n22\t\n23\tThe Staff Engineer / SME Input section is non-empty and takes precedence over the AI-generated\n24\tstrategy sections. Overrides applied:\n25\t\n26\t1. **Component scope**: only odh-dashboard is affected. rhods-operator was removed from the\n27\t   affected components — its HardwareProfile mutating webhook injects the\n28\t   `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label on Notebook CRs and is explicitly out of this STRAT.\n29\t2. **AI-generated \"Proposed Solution\" superseded**: the original solution section's resource\n30\t   columns (\"Requested vs. available CPU/GPU/Memory\"), estimated wait time indicators, historical\n31\t   queue data, and policy information panels are not in the committed HLR list and are out of\n32\t   scope. LocalQueues carry no quota information (quota lives at the ClusterQueue level, often\n33\t   unreadable by data scientists), and Kueue provides no wait-time prediction — only factual\n34\t   elapsed wait time.\n35\t3. **Status model approach**: state-driven from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses,\n36\t   never event-driven from hardcoded progress steps or wildcard/substring event matching. Raw\n37\t   Kueue condition message is always the fallback — never a blank state.\n38\t4. **Non-blocking UX**: development must not block on UXD answers (RHOAIUX-7470). Placeholder\n39\t   copy/treatment ships first; finalized content replaces it later.\n40\t\n41\t## Component Mappings\n42\t\n43\t| Strategy component | Canonical component (`submit.py` vocabulary) | Notes |\n44\t|---|---|---|\n45\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Architecture context file exists (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`) — component is in the platform; no onboarding chain. |\n46\t| UXD design + Content microcopy deliverables (RHOAIUX-7470) | UXD | Delivered via the UXD work stream; no separate Content component exists in the canonical list. |\n47\t| Documentation deliverable | Documentation | Docs team release note / feature docs. |\n48\t\n49\tPassive components: kueue-operator (architecture context exists) requires no code changes — the\n50\tVisibility API is consumed read-only through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s` passthrough.\n51\tValidation of its behavior (including 403 handling) is captured as acceptance criteria on the\n52\tVisibility API epic. No separate team validates it, so no standalone validation epic is generated.\n53\t\n54\t## Investigation Evaluation (Step 3)\n55\t\n56\tAll unknowns were scanned (open questions table, risks, assumptions). Neither qualifies as an\n57\tInvestigation epic:\n58\t\n59\t- **Visibility API RBAC for data scientists** (open question, owner AI Core Platform): the\n60\t  strategy itself resolves the engineering response — code handles 403 gracefully either way, so\n61\t  the answer does not change which epics exist or what they build; it only affects how much polish\n62\t  to invest in the position UI. Modeled as an acceptance criterion (silent 403 degradation) plus a\n63\t  health warning below.\n64\t- **Form of the positive Kueue indicator** (open question, owner UXD / RHOAIUX-7470): a design\n65\t  deliverable produced by an impacted team inside this strategy, explicitly non-blocking\n66\t  (placeholder treatment first). Modeled as a parallel Implementation epic owned by UXD, with a\n67\t  downstream integration epic — not an Investigation.\n68\t\n69\t## Epic List\n70\t\n71\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n72\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n73\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | State-driven Kueue workload status model with eviction-reason distinction and message overrides | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue management indicators on project details and workbenches overview | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile form and popover hardening for Kueue | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n77\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | UX design deliverables for Kueue visibility indicators (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | UXD | P1 |\n78\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | Status message microcopy for Kueue condition/reason overrides (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | Content | P1 |\n79\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Integrate finalized Kueue UX designs and content into the dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n80\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E008 | Documentation for Kueue workload scheduling visibility | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P1 |\n81\t\n82\t## Dependency DAG\n83\t\n84\t```mermaid\n85\tgraph TD\n86\t  E001[\"E001 Status model (P0)\"]\n87\t  E002[\"E002 Visibility API queue position (P1)\"]\n88\t  E003[\"E003 Kueue indicators (P0)\"]\n89\t  E004[\"E004 HP form hardening (P1)\"]\n90\t  E005[\"E005 UX design deliverables (P1)\"]\n91\t  E006[\"E006 Status message microcopy (P1)\"]\n92\t  E007[\"E007 Integrate finalized UX/content (P1)\"]\n93\t  E008[\"E008 Documentation (P1)\"]\n94\t  E001 --> E007\n95\t  E003 --> E007\n96\t  E004 --> E007\n97\t  E005 --> E007\n98\t  E006 --> E007\n99\t  E001 --> E008\n100\t  E002 --> E008\n101\t  E003 --> E008\n102\t  E004 --> E008\n103\t  E005 --> E008\n104\t  E006 --> E008\n105\t  E007 --> E008\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\t## DAG Justification\n109\t\n110\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n111\t|---|---|---|\n112\t| (none among E001–E006) | 14, 15 | E001–E004 live in the same repo but in different areas (status derivation logic, API client, page-level indicators, forms) — parallel; merge coordination is a risk note, not a dependency. The E001/E002 coupling (queue position keys off the QueuingPending state the status model re-derives) is captured as a risk on the Visibility API epic. E005/E006 are different teams with independent inputs — parallel; the RHOAIUX-7470 content review milestone is owned by the microcopy epic (E006), with the UX design epic (E005) participating as reviewer. No epic builds against an artifact another of these produces. |\n113\t| E001 → E007 | 13 | The integration epic swaps the default message-override entries delivered by the status model — it builds against that lookup table. |\n114\t| E003 → E007 | 13 | Final visual treatments are applied to the indicator surfaces delivered by the indicators work. |\n115\t| E004 → E007 | 13 | The HP dropdown info indicator's final treatment is applied to the form surface delivered by the HP hardening work. |\n116\t| E005 → E007 | 13 | Integration consumes the finalized design deliverable (build-against artifact: design spec). |\n117\t| E006 → E007 | 13 | Integration consumes the reviewed microcopy deliverable (build-against artifact: override table content). |\n118\t| E002 ∥ E007 (no edge) | 14 | Queue position display is not UX-gated; no build-against artifact shared. |\n119\t| E001–E007 → E008 | 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy — docs describe what was built. |\n120\t\n121\tNo repo-onboarding, license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics: odh-dashboard is in the\n122\tplatform (architecture context file exists) and no new component or container image is provisioned.\n123\t\n124\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n125\t\n126\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n127\t|---|---|---|\n128\t| HLR-P0-1 Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons | P0 | E001 |\n129\t| HLR-P0-2 Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time | P0 | E001 |\n130\t| HLR-P0-3 Positive Kueue indicator on project details page | P0 | E003 (placeholder treatment), E005 (design), E007 (final integration) |\n131\t| HLR-P0-4 Anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces | P0 | E003 (placeholder treatment), E005 (design), E007 (final integration) |\n132\t| HLR-P0-5 Workload scheduling status from Workload CR conditions with message overrides and raw fallback | P0 | E001 (model + defaults), E006 (reviewed content), E007 (final integration) |\n133\t| HLR-P1-6 Kueue Visibility API queue position with graceful 403 degradation | P1 | E002 |\n134\t| HLR-P1-7 HardwareProfile popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks | P1 | E004 |\n135\t| HLR-P1-8 k8sNameRegex validation on LocalQueue name field | P1 | E004 |\n136\t| HLR-P1-9 Info indicator on HP dropdown in Kueue-managed namespaces | P1 | E004 (placeholder), E005 (design), E007 (final integration) |\n137\t| HLR-P2-10 Structured, extensible status derivation model | P2 | E001 |\n138\t| HLR-P2-11 Status message granularity (WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck states) | P2 | E001, E006 |\n139\t\n140\tFull coverage: all 11 HLRs map to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n141\t\n142\t**Priority-split decisions:**\n143\t- E001 bundles P0-1/P0-2/P0-5 with P2-10/P2-11: the P2 HLRs are the structural status-derivation\n144\t  refactor and message-granularity work on exactly the same implementation surface (the status\n145\t  model) — tightly coupled, not independently shippable. Splitting would duplicate the same data\n146\t  structures. Bundled per Step 4.\n147\t- E003 bundles P0-3/P0-4 (same logical change: Kueue management indicators, same team); E004\n148\t  bundles P1-7/P1-8/P1-9 (same HardwareProfile form/popover hardening area).\n149\t- E005/E006/E007 are prioritized P1 although they refine P0 HLR surfaces (P0-3/P0-4/P0-5). Per the\n150\t  Staff Engineer directive the P0 HLRs are fully delivered by E001/E003 with placeholder/default\n151\t  copy and treatment; the UX/content layer is an explicitly non-blocking refinement, so it does\n152\t  not inherit P0. No P0 epic depends on them, so no priority inversion exists in the DAG.\n153\t\n154\t## Health Warnings\n155\t\n156\t1. **Visibility API RBAC availability (non-gating)**: whether data scientists in RHOAI clusters\n157\t   carry `view`/`edit`/`batch-user` bindings that aggregate Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`\n158\t   is unresolved (owner: AI Core Platform). The code handles 403 either way, but if the bindings\n159\t   are absent, queue position display is effectively admin-only — which would reduce the value of\n160\t   the P1 position UI polish. Tracked as an acceptance criterion (silent degradation) and a risk on\n161\t   the Visibility API epic, not a DAG gate.\n162\t2. **Scope trap — superseded AI-generated solution**: the strategy's AI-generated \"Proposed\n163\t   Solution\" section (resource requested-vs-available columns, estimated wait times, historical\n164\t   queue data, policy panels) contradicts the Staff Engineer scope constraints and the committed\n165\t   HLR list. Those items must not re-enter as acceptance criteria; quota preview is infeasible and\n166\t   Kueue provides no wait-time prediction.\n167\t3. **Content dependency timing**: the finalized UX/content deliverables (RHOAIUX-7470) have no\n168\t   committed date. This is absorbed by design (placeholder-first development); the integration epic\n169\t   simply lands when the deliverables do. Schedule risk, not a structural risk.\n170\t4. **Event-driven status logic replacement**: E001 replaces existing wildcard/substring event\n171\t   matching with a condition-driven model — a rewrite of an existing capability. Rollback safety is\n172\t   handled by the purely-additive/conditional NFR (behavior unchanged when Kueue is not enabled),\n173\t   captured as an acceptance criterion on E001.\n174\t\n175\t## Tiered Delivery\n176\t\n177\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing that gates user-facing\n178\tvalue: the only dependency (UXD finalized designs and content, RHOAIUX-7470) is an internal team\n179\tdeliverable that the strategy explicitly decouples from development via placeholder-first\n180\timplementation, modeled here as parallel epics plus a final integration epic rather than as a\n181\tblocking tier boundary.\n182\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8019f459d0512869","agent_id":"ac74c8e642485881c","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"0817efcf-fabe-443d-9301-60aa36d6c6f9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:44.054Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b028fc677f68cfc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
