{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1bda599d1756e32","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tIntegrate Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`) into the odh-dashboard so\n34\tthe workbenches overview can display the queue position of pending workloads\n35\t(`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via the `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on\n36\tLocalQueues, with silent graceful degradation when the user's RBAC does not permit reading it.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Add a frontend API client for the LocalQueue pending-workloads subresource:\n41\t  `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`.\n42\t- All calls go through the existing `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy using the logged-in user's token\n43\t  (browser → frontend SDK → `/api/k8s` → K8s API), so every call is subject to the user's RBAC\n44\t  permissions.\n45\t- Display the queue position (position in local queue) for workbenches in QueuingPending state in\n46\t  the workbenches overview.\n47\t- Handle a 403 on the Visibility API silently using the existing `getGenericErrorCode` pattern\n48\t  from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx` — position info is supplementary, not critical; no error\n49\t  is surfaced to the user.\n50\t- Reuse the existing workload-to-notebook matching (`buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` in\n51\t  `api/k8s/workloads.ts`) to associate pending-workload positions with workbenches.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has `batch-user` RBAC to the\n56\t  Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is displayed\n57\t  (position in local queue), measured by the position number being present and matching the value\n58\t  from the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n59\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT have RBAC to the\n60\t  Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is silently\n61\t  omitted with no error displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error\n62\t  indicators.\n63\t- All Visibility API requests are issued through the `/api/k8s` passthrough with the logged-in\n64\t  user's token — no privileged impersonation.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-P1-6: Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display (`positionInLocalQueue`,\n69\t  `positionInClusterQueue`) via the `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueue —\n70\t  gracefully degrade on 403.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Whether data scientists in RHOAI clusters receive Kubernetes `view`, `edit`, or `batch-user`\n75\t  ClusterRole bindings that aggregate Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` is an open\n76\t  question owned by AI Core Platform. It is non-gating: the code handles 403 gracefully either\n77\t  way. If the bindings are absent, position display is effectively admin-only, which would reduce\n78\t  the value of further position UI polish.\n79\t- Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`) with the `VisibilityOnDemand`\n80\t  feature gate (Beta, enabled by default since Kueue v0.9) is confirmed available in RHBoK shipped\n81\t  with RHOAI 3.5.\n82\t- Coupling with the status model rebuild: the queue-position display keys off the QueuingPending\n83\t  workload state, which the parallel status-model rebuild work re-derives from Workload CR\n84\t  conditions. That state exists in the dashboard today, so the two efforts run in parallel rather\n85\t  than one blocking the other; however, any change to how QueuingPending is derived or represented\n86\t  must be coordinated at merge time to keep the position display keyed to the correct state.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8019f459d0512869","agent_id":"ac74c8e642485881c","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"88f712bd-246f-47a7-835d-2185ee850c43","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:48.990Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1bda599d1756e32","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
