{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc0b331319a3c26","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue management indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue management indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd Kueue management visibility to the odh-dashboard UI: a positive indicator on the project\n34\tdetails page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, and an anomaly indicator on workbenches in a\n35\tKueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue. Both indicators render conditionally — no\n36\tUI changes when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Positive Kueue indicator on the project details page, shown when the namespace carries the\n41\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, telling users their project uses queue-based\n42\t  scheduling. The exact form (info banner, badge, or label) is a pending UX decision\n43\t  (RHOAIUX-7470); implement with a placeholder treatment that is clearly marked for replacement\n44\t  when the finalized design lands.\n45\t- Anomaly indicator on workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are missing the\n46\t  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (workloads created via GitOps or CLI that bypass Kueue). Do\n47\t  NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every workload in a Kueue-managed namespace — only flag the\n48\t  anomaly.\n49\t- Anomaly detection reuses the namespace `kueue.openshift.io/managed` label and the workload\n50\t  queue-label check; the indicator serves hybrid GitOps + dashboard users.\n51\t- The dashboard remains opinionated (auto-enables Kueue) but explicitly tells users what it is\n52\t  doing; the anomaly indicator never blocks workload creation or any action.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive\n57\t  indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator\n58\t  element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`\n59\t  exists and absent when it does not.\n60\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the\n61\t  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the\n62\t  user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator\n63\t  that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on\n64\t  non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n65\t- The placeholder visual treatments are implemented such that the finalized design treatment can\n66\t  be applied without structural changes to the indicator logic.\n67\t- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not\n68\t  Kueue-managed.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-P0-3: Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has\n73\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n74\t- HLR-P0-4: Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed\n75\t  by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8019f459d0512869","agent_id":"ac74c8e642485881c","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"bacf4de0-40b7-4d55-8e4b-abff99bd9b8c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:49.883Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc0b331319a3c26","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
