atment (info icon / tooltip) for the HardwareProfile dropdown that\n48\t  explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n49\t- Provide UX design input to the status message content review (RHOAIUX-7470); the review\n50\t  milestone itself is owned by the Content team's microcopy deliverable.\n51\t- Deliver design specs that are implementable in the odh-dashboard without structural redesign of\n52\t  the placeholder implementations.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The design decision for the positive Kueue indicator form is made and documented with\n57\t  rationale, and the visual treatment spec is delivered.\n58\t- The anomaly indicator design is delivered and clearly distinguishes non-Kueue workloads without\n59\t  adding per-workload noise in the steady state.\n60\t- The HardwareProfile dropdown info indicator treatment is delivered.\n61\t- Design input for the status message content review (RHOAIUX-7470) is provided to the Content\n62\t  team's microcopy deliverable, which owns completion of the review.\n63\t- All delivered specs can be applied to the existing placeholder implementations without\n64\t  structural changes to indicator logic.\n65\t\n66\t## Notes\n67\t\n68\t- This epic runs in parallel with dashboard engineering work by design — the strategy explicitly\n69\t  states development must not be blocked on UX answers, since the questions concern microcopy and\n70\t  visual treatment, not major redesigns.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-P0-3 (supporting): visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator on the project details\n75\t  page — the indicator itself is delivered by the dashboard engineering work with placeholder\n76\t  treatment.\n77\t- HLR-P0-4 (supporting): anomaly indicator design for non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed\n78\t  namespaces.\n79\t- HLR-P1-9 (supporting): info indicator treatment for the HardwareProfile dropdown.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8019f