k pending/retry\n46\t  states.\n47\t- Structure the deliverable as lookup-table entries keyed by condition/reason, consumable directly\n48\t  by the dashboard's message override table.\n49\t- Complete content review with the UXD team (RHOAIUX-7470).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Override copy is delivered for every known condition/reason combination enumerated by the\n54\t  dashboard status model, each entry keyed by condition type and reason.\n55\t- The copy is reviewed with UXD via RHOAIUX-7470; this epic owns completion of that joint review\n56\t  milestone (the UX design deliverables workstream participates as reviewer).\n57\t- The deliverable is structured as a lookup table that drops into the dashboard's override\n58\t  mechanism without code changes.\n59\t- The copy is written for data scientists (non-Kubernetes-experts): raw Kueue condition messages\n60\t  are unintelligible to that audience, which is the motivation for the overrides.\n61\t- Message lengths fit the dashboard status display constraints.\n62\t\n63\t## Notes\n64\t\n65\t- Engineering is not blocked on this deliverable: the dashboard ships reasonable default overrides\n66\t  first, and the reviewed copy replaces them when available.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-P0-5 (supporting): human-friendly message overrides for workload scheduling status — the\n71\t  override framework and default copy are delivered by the dashboard status model work; this epic\n72\t  delivers the reviewed final wording.\n73\t- HLR-P2-11 (supporting): wording for the improved message granularity (WaitForRecovery vs.\n74\t  WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry states).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8019f459d0512869","agent_id":"ac74c8e642485881c","session_id":"25d8375f-a217-4cdf-8fb9-81de62a8ecf8","uuid":"ce216672-bd2f-45af-85ff-14b5c9c43e95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:54.622Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af7e8497be06a62d","permission_decision":{"decisi